# ADR 0012: Program schema versioning built in from v1

**Date:** 2026-08-02
**Status:** Accepted

## Context
Program structure will evolve over time — new prescription fields 
(RIR targets, tempo, superset grouping), changes to rep range 
representation, etc. Retrofitting version handling later is 
expensive.

## Decision
Every `Program` entity has an integer `schemaVersion` field, set 
at creation. The top-level JSON export has its own 
`forge_version`. Both are used to trigger migrations when the app 
encounters older data.

## Alternatives considered
- **Add versioning when first needed:** Guarantees a painful 
  migration when the first breaking change happens.

## Consequences
- One-line field on Program adds negligible complexity.
- Import layer can detect and migrate old exports.
- SwiftData's own migration system handles storage-level schema 
  changes; the version field handles semantic changes.

